    "value": "none\n\nClient Services is the internal customer service team at Zimmermann. In Magento today, they primarily use the platform to support client-facing enquiries, troubleshoot account and order issues.\n\n**Primary purpose in Magento:** Client Services uses Magento mainly as a reference and support tool rather than a transaction-processing system. Their work focuses on helping customers by viewing order details, generating tax invoices, checking account-related information, and investigating issues.\n\n**Summary:** Magento is most valuable to this team when they need a fast view of customer and order information, especially for troubleshooting and tax invoice access.\n\nPersona snapshot\n================\n\n| Field | Details |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Persona** | Client Services |\n| **Role** | Internal customer service team supporting shoppers with order, account, returns, and troubleshooting queries |\n| **Primary goal** | Resolve customer issues quickly using Magento as a source of order and customer information |\n| **Typical use of Magento** | Order lookup, tax invoice generation, password reset, wishlist troubleshooting, return visibility, shipment reference, and limited promotions support |\n| **What they do not use Magento for** | Order cancellation, creating returns, most customer detail updates |\n\nKey Magento activities\n======================\n\nOrder management and troubleshooting\n------------------------------------\n\nThe most commonly used area is **Sales > Orders**. This gives Client Services an overview of the order and helps them answer customer questions quickly.\n\n* View order details and status breakdown\n* Confirm whether the customer was logged in when placing the order or a guest\n* Use failed or incomplete order records for troubleshooting, e.g. cases where payment was not received\n* Edit Billing and Shipping Address on orders\n* See if credit was used as part of payment\n* Use Magento as a starting point for shipment investigation\n\nnote320830b5e3ca\n\n**Important:** Client Services can edit shipping and billing addresses in Magento, but changes do not automatically flow through to OMS. In practice, billing address edits are the more common use case, usually for tax-related corrections.\n\n**Important:** Client Services can edit shipping and billing addresses in Magento, but changes do not automatically flow through to OMS. In practice, billing address edits are the more common use case, usually for tax-related corrections.\n\n**Note on to-be: In SFCC we are not syncing back the order statuses - so only the initial orders submitted will be visible. They cannot edit the order’s address details in SFCC. For full order status, CS should troubleshoot in Newstore.**\n\nTax invoice generation\n----------------------\n\nOne of the most important Magento functions for Client Services is generating tax invoices. This appears to be a key action they still rely on Magento.\n\n* Tax invoices are accessed through the invoice section of the order\n* Client Services can use the print function to generate the invoice\n* For Australia, the invoice includes Zimmermann's ABN\n* Other receipts available in other platforms do not include the same tax invoice detail\n\n**Callout:** Magento is currently the only source for tax invoices, which makes it operationally important for Client Services even where other systems hold overlapping order data.\n\n**Note on to-be: Ideally this is not happening in SFCC but again, should happen in Newstore. Advice is to check if possible in Newstore - in SFCC this is not out of the box but custom build.**\n\nCustomer account support\n------------------------\n\nMagento is used to help with basic customer account troubleshooting, especially where the issue directly impacts the customer's ability to shop or access their account.\n\n* Locate a customer profile by email address\n* Trigger password reset emails for customers who cannot log in\n* View customer order history\n* View wishlist contents to help troubleshoot product or size or inventory issues\n* View customer group status, such as Gold VIP, for support and troubleshooting\n\nAlthough Magento displays some account-related information, Client Services does **not** generally maintain broader customer profile details there.\n\n**Boundary:** Client details beyond billing and shipping address are typically updated in Omneo, not in Magento.\n\n**Note on to-be: In SFCC they can view customer profile, reset password, view the wishlist and group status. Order history again is limited to only the orders initial status - no further order status updates beyond submission.**\n\nShipment visibility\n-------------------\n\nMagento has historically been useful for shipment lookups because it shows tracking information and carrier details. At present, this information is not always fully reliable due to changes in surrounding systems, so the team may need to check another tool as well.\n\n* Review shipment details from the order\n* Check tracking references and links where available\n* Use Magento as an initial reference point before moving to other systems if needed\n\n**Note on to-be: In SFCC they cannot view the shipment details on an order - they need to start doing this in Newstore - carrier system**\n\nReturns visibility\n------------------\n\nClient Services can view return information in Magento, including return shipment details and the stated return outcome.\n\n* See returned items\n* View return reason or resolution, e.g. size is too small\n* Review shipment details connected to the return\n\nHistorically, the team could manually submit returns through Magento. That process has changed.\n\nnotef137ee3da239\n\n**Current state:** If Client Services needs to help complete a return, they would do so in Narvar rather than Magento.\n\n**Current state:** If Client Services needs to help complete a return, they would do so in Narvar rather than Magento.\n\n**Note on to-be: In SFCC they cannot view returns - this should be in Narvar**\n\nPromotions and goodwill gestures\n--------------------------------\n\nClient Services has limited involvement in promotions within Magento, and this tends to be regional and infrequent.\n\n* In Australia, Finance typically generates digital gift vouchers for customer use, outside of Magento\n* In Hong Kong, Magento may be used to create a voucher or discount code specifically for Gold VIP customer credit scenarios. This may additionally happen in Middle East store - this is a small part of the customers\n* This is mainly used when website or regional system limitations prevent the normal credit or voucher flow\n* These cases are rare and not part of regular daily work\n\n**Note on to-be: In SFCC they can set up promotion code for the customers**\n\nNotify Me support\n-----------------\n\nMagento can also support customer conversations around product interest and out-of-stock communication.\n\n* See what notifications or emails a client has received for item availability in some scenarios\n\nThis helps the team respond when a customer says they expected an update or is having trouble purchasing an item they previously saved.\n\n**Note on to-be: since SFCC sends out the notify me, they can see this email trail on the customer profile**\n\nWhat Client Services does outside Magento\n=========================================\n\n| Activity | Current system or approach |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Order cancellation** | Handled in NewStore, not Magento. |\n| **Returns submission** | Handled in Narvar rather than Magento under the current process. |\n| **Broader customer detail updates** | Handled in Omneo rather than Magento. |\n| **Some shipment follow-up** | May require another operational system while OMS updates are in transition. |\n| **Digital gift vouchers** | In Australia, typically generated by Finance rather than by Client Services in Magento. |\n\nKey observations and implications\n=================================\n\n* Magento is primarily a **visibility and troubleshooting tool** for Client Services\n* The most business-critical capability appears to be **tax invoice generation**\n* Several workflows are split across Magento and other systems, which creates operational complexity\n* Some editable data in Magento does not sync automatically downstream, which may create risk or confusion\n* Promotions use cases exist, but they are niche and region-specific rather than core to the persona\n\n:mag:1f50d🔍#EAE6FF\n\n**Persona takeaway:** As a **Client Services** user, I want a fast and accurate view of customer, order, invoice, shipment, and return information, so that I can resolve customer issues efficiently without switching across multiple systems unnecessarily.\n\nTo-be with SFCC\n===============\n\n| **Activity** | **SFCC** | **Omneo** | **Narvar** | **NewStore** | **Change for CS?** | **Comment** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Customer Profile:** Reset Password |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n| **Customer Profile:** View Wishlist |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n| **Customer Profile:** Edit Customer Details |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n| **Customer Profile:** View Loyalty Status |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n| **Order Management:** View Order History |  |  |  |  | Yes |  |\n| **Order Management:** View Order Detail |  |  |  |  | Yes |  |\n| **Order Management:** Edit Order Detail |  |  |  |  | Yes | incl. Shipping / Billing Address |\n| **Order Management:** Troubleshoot Failed / Incomplete Orders |  |  |  |  | No | incl. checking if customer placed order as Guest or logged in |\n| **Order Management:** View Shipment Information |  |  |  |  | Yes | Shipment details are available in NewStore |\n| **Returns:** View Return Details |  |  |  |  | Yes | Return details are not stored in NewStore - they’d have to view them in Narvar/global-e |\n| **Tax Invoice:** Generate tax invoice |  |  |  |  | Yes | Tax invoice generation in NewStore |\n| **Promotions:** Edge Case - Gold VIP voucher creation |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n| **Customer Notifications** - Overview of Notify Me Emails |  |  |  |  | No |  |\n\nOpen items / Decision tracker\n=============================\n\n| **Topic** | **Outcome** | **Who** | **Date** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Tax invoice generation in NewStore? | Yes, this is a supported functionality | @Lucy Fu (Unlicensed) | 19-06-2026 |\n| Shipment visibility in NewStore? | Yes, this is a supported functionality | @Lucy Fu (Unlicensed) | 19-06-2026 |\n| Returns visbility in NewStore? | No, returns creation happens in Narvar for domestic, global-E for international - only when the return is completely processed - will the order status be marked as “Returned” in NewStore. This means Client Services would have to view returns in Narvar/Global-e | @Lucy Fu (Unlicensed) | 19-06-2026 |\n|  |  |  |  |"
  }
}"}

