    "value": "**Status: DRAFT — working document, not yet reviewed.** Purpose: reconcile every place \"our integrations\" are listed, before we cut any Jira epics or action items. Once this is settled, the output becomes epics (one per integration with real PWA-side work) with action items/open questions as sub-tasks. Please comment/edit directly — nothing here is final.\n\nWhy this page exists\n--------------------\n\nTim asked \"are these all our integrations?\" while we were scoping Jira epics from the repo's consolidated open-items list. The answer turned out to be no — there are **four sources**, each with a different count, and none of them agree:\n\n| Source | Location | Count | Organising principle |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Architecture matrix | repo `.claude/docs/architecture.md` (Third-Party Integrations table) | 28 | One row per vendor — the most complete single technical list |\n| Integration status tracker | repo `.claude/docs/memory/projectState.md` | 18 | Mock / Live / Not-started tracker — a *subset* of the 28 |\n| Consolidated open items | repo `.claude/docs/design/openItems.md` | 18 (40 items) | Only vendors with a known client-confirmation gap |\n| Integration Register (this Confluence section) | 9 child pages (Product, PDP, Checkout, Order History, Order Details, My Account, Store Details, Inventory Sync, MuleSoft Overview) | 30 unique INT-IDs (parent page claims 34) | One row per **page where a vendor is used** — the same vendor can (and does) appear on multiple pages under the same INT-ID |\n\nThe repo and Confluence were clearly built independently and have since drifted. Below is the reconciliation.\n\nMaster vendor list (union of all four sources)\n----------------------------------------------\n\nLegend: ✅ present · — not present · **NEW** = not in the repo at all\n\n| Vendor / System | architecture.md | projectState.md status | openItems.md | Confluence INT-ID(s) | Confluence status | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SFCC | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (2 items) | — (platform itself) | — |  |\n| MuleSoft | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (4 items) | INT-033 | Under Review | ~~ID collision — INT-033 also used for Measmerize~~**Resolved 2026-07-07** — Measmerize moved to INT-034 on the PDP register page. |\n| NewStore OMS | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | INT-014 | Under Review (Confirmed on Store Details) | architecture.md flags an explicit open item (customer-ID mechanism on read path) that never made it into openItems.md. Confluence has *four* separate open questions across PDP / Order History / Order Details / Inventory Sync — all more granular than the repo. |\n| AP21 | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | INT-013 | Under Review | architecture.md says \"feed cadence/field set TBC\"; Confluence separately flags attribute-taxonomy ownership and OCI location-group IDs. Different aspects of the same gap — worth merging. |\n| Omneo | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (3 items, \"hard blockers\") | INT-023 | Under Review | Confluence's open item (Omneo *API* auth method, SFCC-side) is distinct from the repo's (iframe embed auth, front-end side) — both real, both needed. |\n| Emarsys | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item) | INT-024 | **Not Required** | Confluence confirms: no direct SFCC↔Emarsys integration, routes via Omneo. Consistent with repo. |\n| Adyen | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-005 | **Confirmed** | Confluence shows this further along than the repo's \"Not started\" status suggests — worth a status sync. |\n| Global-e | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-007 (checkout), INT-021 (post-purchase order status), INT-022 (returns portal) | Confirmed (007) / Under Review (021, 022) | Confluence splits one vendor into 3 tracked surfaces; repo treats it as one. New open questions: order-sync/reconciliation mechanism (007), returns-link source-system flag (021), how SFCC distinguishes international vs domestic orders (022) — none of these are in the repo. |\n| Booxi | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (4 items) | — **not in register at all** | — | Confluence register has no page/row for Booxi. |\n| Narvar | ✅ (one row) | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-018 (EDD/Promise), INT-019 (CARE/tracking), INT-020 (returns) | Under Review (all 3) | Same split-vs-single pattern as Global-e. New questions: is EDD real-time API or SFCC-rule-based (018); tracking URL source (019); return-eligibility check location (020, this one *is* echoed in the repo's ENH-014 unresolved dependency). |\n| Contentful | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (3 items) | INT-002 | Under Review | Confluence's open questions (content-type mapping, PDP vs PLP structure) read as more basic/early than where the repo's actual build has gotten to (content-type sync script exists, ShoppableImage component built) — Confluence looks stale here. |\n| Vimeo | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | INT-003 | Under Review |  |\n| Didomi | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-011 | **Confirmed** |  |\n| Google Maps API | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (1 item) | INT-009 (as \"Google Places API\") | **Confirmed** |  |\n| GTM | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | INT-031 (as \"GA4 / GTM\") | Under Review | Appears on almost every register page — highest-frequency INT-ID. |\n| Optimizely Web | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (1 item) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| Crazy Egg | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (3 items) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| Avalara | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item; looked resolved) | INT-008 | Under Review | Repo reads as settled (cartridge, EU domestic confirmed); Confluence still has the integration *method* itself open (direct SFCC↔Avalara vs via MuleSoft). Real conflict, not just a gap. |\n| GiveX | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (3 items) | INT-012 (as \"Give-X\") | Under Review | Consistent with repo (NewStore adaptor for redemption/balance). |\n| Transperfect | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | — **not in register at all** | — | architecture.md flags \"translation workflow trigger TBD\" — a real open item that's in neither openItems.md nor Confluence. |\n| Inside Chat | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (0 items — \"no open items\") | INT-027 | Under Review | Confluence actually has 3 open questions (chat suppression rules, which attributes get passed, page scope) that openItems.md says don't exist. openItems.md is wrong here, not Confluence. |\n| Zendesk | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | — (no PWA item; \"Not an embedded integration\") | INT-026 | **Conflicting** — \"Under Review\" on Order Details, \"Not Required\" on My Account | Internal Confluence inconsistency, independent of the repo. |\n| Google reCAPTCHA | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| GDPR cartridge | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | — (no PWA item) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| Shippit / Ordoro | ✅ (one row) | — (missing from tracker) | — (no PWA item) | INT-015 (Shippit/StarShipit), INT-016 (Ordoro) | Not Required (both) | Confluence splits by market (AU/HK vs US/UK/EU) and flags \"confirm Ordoro is not being replaced by NewStore at go-live\" — a real open question absent from the repo. |\n| Google Business API | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item; looked resolved) | INT-017 | Under Review | Repo reads as settled (\"PWA renders only\"); Confluence still questions whether it's API-fed or a manual export, and who owns the Google Business profile. |\n| Feedonomics | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item) | — **not in register** (but see Lengow, below) | — |  |\n| Measmerize | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | INT-034 ✅ *(fixed 2026-07-07 — was mislabelled INT-033, colliding with MuleSoft)* | Under Review |  |\n| SearchSpring | — not in repo | — | — | INT-001 | **Not Required** | Confluence-only: evaluated and rejected in favour of SFCC Einstein. Consistent with the repo's Einstein-based search decision — just never made it into the repo as a \"considered and rejected\" note. |\n| HotJar | — not in repo | — | — | INT-030 | **Not Required** (\"not used anymore\") | Confluence-only, rejected. No action needed. |\n| Lexer CDP | — not in repo | — | — | INT-025 | **Not Required** (\"no direct integration with SFCC\") | **NEW** — a customer data platform fed by daily batch export from Omneo. No PWA-side work, but worth a one-line mention in architecture.md for completeness. |\n| Lengow | — not in repo | — | — | INT-028 | Under Review | **NEW** — exports SFCC catalogue to Google Shopping / Facebook / Pinterest. This looks like it may be the **same underlying need as** `Feedonomics` in the repo (\"product feed for downstream marketing channels\"), described as two different vendors. Needs a decision: same vendor under two names, a replacement, or genuinely two separate feeds? |\n| New Relic | — (mentioned only as ops tooling, not in the integration matrix) | — | — | INT-032 | Not Required | APM/monitoring, not a business integration — its absence from the repo's integration matrix is arguably correct; flagging only because it does appear in the Confluence register. |\n| \"Federated Login\" / SSO across storefronts | — (see cross-storefront session notes) | — | — (tracked as \"SSO scope CRM-001\" unresolved dependency instead) | — **not in the register at all** | — | Same underlying gap tracked under a different name in the repo. No dedicated Confluence page for it. |\n\nData-integrity issues to resolve (independent of the epic-creation question)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1. **~~INT-033 collision.~~RESOLVED 2026-07-07.** Measmerize moved from INT-033 (colliding with MuleSoft on the Product/Inventory Sync pages) to INT-034 on the PDP register page.\n2. **Missing ID block: 004, 006, 010, 029.** Never appear across any of the 9 register pages. Either reserved for integrations not yet documented in the register (my guess: Booxi, Transperfect, reCAPTCHA, Optimizely, Crazy Egg, GDPR cartridge — all six are real repo integrations with no register page at all), or genuinely unused. (034 is no longer a gap — now assigned to Measmerize.)\n3. **Zendesk status conflict.** \"Under Review\" on the Order Details page, \"Not Required\" on the My Account page, for what should be the same underlying integration decision.\n4. **Lengow vs. Feedonomics.** Likely the same business need described independently in Confluence (Lengow) and the repo (Feedonomics) — needs a same-or-different call before either gets a Jira epic.\n5. **Six repo integrations have no Confluence register page at all:** Booxi, Transperfect, Google reCAPTCHA, GDPR cartridge, Optimizely Web, Crazy Egg.\n6. **Contentful and Avalara read as further along / more settled in the repo than Confluence shows** — worth a status sync so Confluence isn't acted on as if it's current when the repo reflects newer decisions (e.g. Avalara's EU-domestic confirmation from 2026-06-19 isn't reflected in the Confluence \"Under Review\" status).\n\nRecommendation for Jira epic scoping (open question — see below)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTwo options, not yet decided:\n\n* **Option A — one epic per vendor** (~24–28 epics), matching architecture.md's granularity. Simpler; matches how the repo already documents things.\n* **Option B — one epic per INT-ID / vendor-feature combination** (~30+ now the collision/gaps are being fixed), matching the Confluence register's granularity. More precise for vendors like Global-e and Narvar, which have genuinely distinct sub-integrations with separate owners and timelines.\n\nOpen questions for review\n-------------------------\n\n* [ ] Epic granularity: Option A or B above?\n* [x] ~~Who resolves the INT-033 collision~~ — done 2026-07-07 (Measmerize → INT-034). Still open: who resolves the 004/006/010/029 ID gaps — an Accenture-side Confluence cleanup task, separate from the Jira epic work?\n* [ ] Lengow vs. Feedonomics — same vendor, replacement, or two real feeds?\n* [ ] Should the six repo-only integrations (Booxi, Transperfect, reCAPTCHA, GDPR cartridge, Optimizely, Crazy Egg) get register pages added, or is the repo sufficient for those?\n* [ ] Confirm whether `projectState.md`'s status tracker should be expanded to cover all 28 (currently missing 10) as a separate repo-side fix.\n\n---\n\n*Compiled 2026-07-07 by cross-referencing* `.claude/docs/architecture.md`*,* `.claude/docs/memory/projectState.md`*,* `.claude/docs/design/openItems.md`*, and this Confluence section's 9 Integration Register pages (Integration Overview, Product, PDP, Checkout, Order History, Order Details, My Account, Store Details, Inventory Sync) plus the MuleSoft Integration — Overview page. Last edited 2026-07-07: INT-033/Measmerize collision resolved.*"
